WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.630
- E-mails are arguably still
the most important medium

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.480
of professional communication
in most corporates.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.320
But writing a strong E-mail is not easy.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.220
It's really a craft, a skill
that needs to be trained

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.900
and developed and practiced.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.570
So welcome to another coffee break

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.530
here on my channel "Firm Learning,"

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.190
I'm a former McKinsey consultant,

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.920
and on my channel, I want to help you

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.770
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.990
And today, I wanna talk about

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.270
writing effective and
well-structured E-mails.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.170
So without further ado,
let's jump into it.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.440
I prepared an E-mail here
as a practical example,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.930
and now we can together improve.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.140
Let me briefly read out the E-mail to you.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.340
Subject : Summary of Kick-off,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.010
Dear team, thank you
for your time last week

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.843
in the kick-off,

00:00:39.843 --> 00:00:40.820
and looking forward to meet you again

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.690
in our first Jour Fixe next Tuesday,

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.760
Paul, can you please schedule it,

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.490
and also our monthly SteerCos?

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:46.600
I very much enjoyed our discussion

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.100
on what initiatives to focus on

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.610
for the "New Markets" project.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.820
We decided to not further
pursue opportunities

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.160
in the Nordics or Eastern Europe.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.210
We agreed to focus on Spain

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.576
for a pilot for our CAVOC product line,

00:00:56.576 --> 00:00:58.800
(goal: 20 EUR mn revenue in 6 months).

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.160
We also need to conduct
consumer focus groups in Germany

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.400
to develop new product
variations until end of year.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.530
In addition, we want to
reduce our engagement

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.520
in the French market.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.350
We therefore want to close
down our sales offices,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.530
but make sure the key
accounts can still be served

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.260
from our European account managers.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.093
As the first step,

00:01:13.093 --> 00:01:14.220
I suggest we structure
all these initiatives

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.120
into a project plan.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.410
Carla, can you please set one up

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.900
for our first Jour Fixe next week?

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:18.733
Please, everyone,

00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:20.190
be well prepared for
our Jour Fixe meetings.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.520
I expect to receive regular updates

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.040
from the Sales, Marketing,
and Product team leads

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:23.873
in these meetings.

00:01:23.873 --> 00:01:26.230
Let's make sure we are able
to provide meaningful updates

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.130
to our board in the monthly SteerCos.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.330
Thanks, everyone! Best, Louise.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.650
So while this E-mail is
not completely horrible,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.070
there are for sure several things

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.720
that can be improved significantly.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.540
And the first is the subject line.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.970
So here it says "Summary of Kick-off,"

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.690
where that's not wrong, but
of course, it's quite generic.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:42.523
As a professional,

00:01:42.523 --> 00:01:45.000
you might deal with different
projects at the same time.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.470
It's always better to be
a little bit more precise,

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.040
more specific, that you
directly have the context

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.200
of such an E-mail in the inbox.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.873
So maybe rather write something like

00:01:53.873 --> 00:01:57.210
"[Project:"New Markets"]
Summary Kick-off,"

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.780
just to provide this context.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.760
Let's now talk about the first
paragraph of your E-mail.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.150
Here, you should make sure

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.190
to always have two things included.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.360
First, provide some context.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.370
What is this about?

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.460
What is the context of
what you're writing in?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.650
And then, second,

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.870
also try to summarize
what exactly you want.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.770
So if you want to schedule
a meeting with someone,

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.750
don't just write this in the
last sentence of the E-mail,

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.060
but write this in the first paragraph.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.230
This is also the idea of
"Top-down Communication."

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.490
If you have no idea what
top down communication is,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.490
I made available about
that in the past as well.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.410
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.070
And in this example,
probably what makes sense,

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.150
just to provide an outline
of what you will do here,

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.080
so you will summarize what
has happened in the kickoff,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.700
and what the key topics are
that you will write about.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.730
Again, this provides important context.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.020
Another person knows what to expect

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.760
when looking at the rest of the E-mail.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.530
So let's next talk about
this structure of an E-mail.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:52.370
The core of every good
E-mail is a good structure.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.380
Notice how here

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:56.070
the E-mail is structured
in different paragraphs,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.090
but these paragraphs do not seem to follow

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.610
any logical organization principle.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.450
The next paragraph
talks about initiatives.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.600
First, it mentions things

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.590
that the team does not want to focus on,

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.500
the Nordics or Eastern Europe.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.260
Then it talks about an initiative

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.890
that the team does want to focus on.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.320
Here, Spain for a pilot.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.980
The third paragraph, once
again, talks about initiatives,

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.500
first about what is supposed
to happen in Germany,

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.480
then what is supposed to happen in France,

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.180
and then it is mixed with
information on to-do's.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.700
And then the last paragraph, again,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.260
talks about your fixed meetings,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.170
the expectations toward these meetings,

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.970
and then also some info
on the monthly SteerCos

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.080
that are apparently
supposed to take place.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.330
So let's go over different
things that can be improved here.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.330
And first, let's think
about the logical groups,

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.668
the logical categories that
you want to talk about.

00:03:37.668 --> 00:03:38.501
So in this E-mail,

00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:39.870
there are three types of
information apparently

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.490
that the person wants to communicate.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.440
First, the Focus Initiatives
that are supposed to happen.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.230
Second, the Meeting Schedule,

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.580
what types of meetings are
supposed to take place.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.170
And then third, the Next Steps.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.740
What are the to-do's that
the team members have?

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.790
And when coming up with
these logical categories,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.670
always think of the MECE Principle,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.300
that is, of course, also
applicable here as well,

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.407
when coming up with these groups.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.770
And if you have no idea
what the MECE Principle is,

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.110
it's a structured principle

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.070
that is very commonly used in consulting,

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.450
in professional services.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.890
I made a video about that in the past,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.310
that I will link it somewhere above here.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.470
Check it out to learn more.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.720
Next, try to use bullet-point
format whenever possible,

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:18.360
avoid writing long sentences,

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.800
like you would write paragraphs in a book.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.710
You need far more words to
say the very same things.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.260
Take out words by using
bullet-point format.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.740
And that, again, makes
it far easier to process

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.070
for the person reading this.

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.660
Another little technique that you can use

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.380
just to increase the clarity

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.970
and provide more structure of a E-mail,

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.040
is to go beyond just writing bullets,

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.570
but letting the bullets always
start with 1, 2, 3 words,

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.740
that serve as a little
subheader for the bullets,

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.730
because now, everyone, when
they read these bullets,

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.750
they don't even need to
read it word by word,

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.090
but just for reading one or two words,

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.160
they have an idea what this is about,

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.110
can decide for themselves
if there's some errors

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.020
that they don't even wanna read,

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.560
because it's not so relevant for them,

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.470
but others that they
wanna read more about.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.690
Next, let's talk about
distributing to-do's,

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.880
distributing the next steps to your team,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.550
and an error that I often see,

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.600
and I think it's often quite dangerous,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.370
is if you want that someone in the team

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.780
does certain things, you just,
in the middle of the E-mail,

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.100
somewhere mention their name, right?

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.460
And of course, if these people,

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.890
very carefully read the whole E-mail,

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.380
they might spot their name,

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.380
and they might spot here the information,

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.790
that this is what they need to do.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.400
But in general, I think
it's a good practice,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.640
that whenever you want to
address someone in an E-mail,

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.570
and that person's
supposed to do something,

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.180
you bold that name, right?

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.890
So in the middle of the E-mail,
you make that name bold,

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.520
because then, of course, the
person will quite directly see

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.480
that this is where you
write about the person,

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.260
and can then also read on
the associated to-do's,

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.530
tasks, things that you
want the person to do.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.950
Let's talk about two additional tips

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.550
that are maybe not directly
related to this example E-mail,

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.900
but the first thing that
bothers me quite a lot

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.540
is this E-mail Ping
Pong that often happens

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.720
if you wanna schedule
a meeting with someone,

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.800
because what often happens is,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.830
that one person proposes dates,

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.270
then you need to check in your calendar,

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.340
propose other dates,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.467
and then goes back and forth.

00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:03.680
And so, to avoid making this
process even more complicated,

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.000
make it a good habit of yours,

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.030
that whenever you ask for a meeting,

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.860
always start with some first suggestions

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.260
that you directly share.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.470
And of course, now there are
many more modern mechanisms

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.630
with meeting links, schedule links,

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.370
that can speed up this process even more.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.550
And the second little suggestion

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.910
is the Push for Action in these E-mails,

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.580
because often you have the
bit unpleasant situation,

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.250
that maybe you ask a question
or waiting for feedback,

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.770
and the people aren't replying,

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.100
you don't know, do they still
have a point to share or not,

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:30.933
and so on.

00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:33.570
And a little technique that
I find often quite effective,

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:37.150
is to always then mix your
E-mails with little deadlines.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.900
So maybe write something in the end.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.530
So if you have any feedback on that

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:42.720
or any other point you want to add,

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:46.010
please let us know until tomorrow 2:00 PM.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.790
And if you don't hear anything from them

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.880
until tomorrow 2:00 PM,
then you let them know

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.000
that you assume that
this E-mail is all right.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:52.980
Now, all that being said,

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.580
we all know that the number of E-mails

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.600
that is written in many
professional jobs is far too high,

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.800
the number of E-mails we receive
can really be overwhelming.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.330
So let me share three tips,

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.220
what some things are
that you should avoid,

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.800
when not to write an E-mail.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.770
And I think the first is,

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:09.070
whenever you just wanna
share one or two lines,

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.160
a casual thought,

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.730
nothing that needs to be forwarded

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.040
and needs to be acted on,

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.127
rather avoid E-mails.

00:07:14.127 --> 00:07:17.640
And many companies have
solutions like Microsoft Teams,

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:21.080
Select, Google Chat, and
similar solutions in place,

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.480
rather use them,

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.530
and rather don't write an E-mail

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.220
when it's not absolutely necessary.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.540
Second, to be careful

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:30.410
when you wanna use E-mails
to escalate things.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.760
We all know this feeling,

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.970
something bothers you, a little bit angry,

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.260
so let's write an E-mail,

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:38.210
put lots of people on CC, and complain.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.280
So of course, these are
often also political games,

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.113
that I don't wanna say

00:07:41.113 --> 00:07:43.420
that this is always the wrong thing to do,

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:44.790
but just one tip of advice

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.800
that actually I picked up
from a high school teacher

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.770
back in the day,

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.640
is that that person told me,

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:50.630
when you are angry,

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.990
when you really just wanna
say something to someone,

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.950
when you want to write such a message,

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.410
sleep over it for one night,

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:00.310
just take a break, sleep
over it for one night.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.170
If the next day, you still feel like that,

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.980
that this is the right
thing to do, then go for it.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.157
But often, the next day, you
see things far different.

00:08:07.157 --> 00:08:08.640
You feel different about it.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:09.730
And then you might even regret

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.500
having written such an
E-mail the last day.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:12.333
And then third tip,

00:08:12.333 --> 00:08:14.630
I picked up from a partner
I used to work with,

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.417
that person once told me,

00:08:16.417 --> 00:08:20.750
"Good news in writing,
bad news in-person."

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.410
So if you have a good news to share,

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.210
something great that maybe
you did or your team achieved,

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.540
write an E-mail about that, why?

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.270
Because you wanna make it permanent,

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.300
because you want to give the
recipient the opportunity,

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.130
potentially, to forward the
good news to other people,

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.360
share the good message.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.193
And then this, of course,

00:08:37.193 --> 00:08:39.060
will be something that will
often be positive for you.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:42.170
On the other hand, avoid
putting bad news in writing.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:45.110
Maybe you did a mistake, you
need to come clean on it,

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.940
for these things, don't write an E-mail.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.080
Whenever possible, pick up the phone,

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.640
have a face-to-face conversation

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.314
with the person you wanna talk to.

00:08:52.314 --> 00:08:53.390
And here, for the very same reasons,

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.600
you don't wanna make it
too easy for that person,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.120
just to forward that
E-mail to other people,

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.360
making it very salient,

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.900
what you did, what went wrong,

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.080
you don't want the person hover you later

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.370
in their E-mail inbox,
search for your name,

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.030
and then just, by chance,
finding this E-mail again,

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.670
reminding them of the
things that maybe went bad,

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.380
the things that you did wrong in the past.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.260
So of course, this might be
a little bit oversimplified

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.320
for some situations,

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.457
but in general, the rule of thumb is,

00:09:17.457 --> 00:09:20.790
"Good news in writing,
bad news in-person."

